speechtext:
I have
looked through the supplementary estimates to see if there is anything in connection with immigration, and I find that there is not. Therefore I cannot pursue what I had in mind. However I would draw the attention of the appropriate minister to a leading article in this morning's Globe and Mail which calls for an explanation by the government with respect to the treatment of a Chinese lady by Canadian immigration authorities. As the newspaper puts it, the treatment accorded that young lady is quite different from the statement made by the Prime Minister on the occasion of the visit of Madame Chiang Kai-shek to this city. If it is true, it does not reflect any-
100-126}
